     1,
     "Hi,\r<br>\r<br>I created a bubble chart using ggplot.  The points represent deviations \r<br>of a client rating from a competitor rating on a set of product \r<br>attributes.  I want to color each bubble so that if the deviation from \r<br>the client is positive, the bubble is green; otherwise red.  How do I \r<br>color each bubble differently?  The fill command for geom_point only \r<br>takes one color.  I need two.\r<br>\r<br>Thanks,\r<br>\r<br>Walt\r<br>\r<br>________________________\r<br>\r<br>Walter R. Paczkowski, Ph.D.\r<br>Data Analytics Corp.\r<br>44 Hamilton Lane\r<br>Plainsboro, NJ 08536\r<br>________________________\r<br>(V) <a href=\"tel:(609)%20936-8999\" value=\"+16099368999\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">609-936-8999</a>\r<br>(F) <a href=\"tel:(609)%20936-3733\" value=\"+16099363733\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">609-936-3733</a>\r<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">wa...@dataanalyticscorp.com</a>\r<br><a href=\"http://www.dataanalyticscorp.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.dataanalyticscorp.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375415011000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ky8CrFnizAMYtcaCeV-wL\">www.dataanalyticscorp.com</a>\r<br>_____________________________________________________\r<br>\r<br>"
